hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"216","A`ūdhu bikalimāti ‘llāhit-tāmmāti min sharri mā khalaq. I seek refuge in the Perfect Words of Allah from the evil of what He has created. Reference: Muslim 4/2080."
"217","Yukabbiru ʿalā kulli sharafin thalātha takbīrāt, thumma yaqūl: Lā ilāha illā Allāhu waḥdahu lā sharīka lahu, lahu al-mulku wa lahu al-ḥamdu, wa huwa ʿalā kulli shay'in qadīr. Āyibūn, tā'ibūn, ʿābidūn, li-Rabbinā ḥāmidūn. Ṣadaqa Allāhu waʿdahu, wa naṣara ʿabdahu, wa hazama al-aḥzāba waḥdahu.. He says \Allāhu Akbar\"" (Takbīr) three times at every elevated place"","" then says: There is no god but Allah alone"","" with no partner. To Him belongs sovereignty"","" and to Him belongs all praise"","" and He is over all things competent. We are returning"","" repenting"","" worshipping"","" and praising our Lord. Allah has fulfilled His promise"","" aided His servant"","" and defeated the confederates alone."""
